# These files are byte-exact evidence, not source code.
#
# `*_original-production-applied.sql` must hash to the SHA-256 recorded in
# docs/APPLIED_LEDGER.md at apply time — that equality is the only proof the
# preserved copy is genuine, and it is asserted by
# apps/web/lib/guards/historical-migration-audit-trail.test.ts.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line normalisation so the working-tree bytes are
# identical on every platform. Without it git would check these out as CRLF on
# Windows, changing the hash and failing the integrity guard.
*_original-production-applied.sql -text
